# Docs Media Hosting

All images and screenshots in planton.ai documentation use the Cloudflare R2 CDN. Never use local paths, GitHub URLs, or other hosting.

## CDN Base URL

```
https://assets.planton.ai/site/images/
```

## URL Structure for Docs

Documentation images follow the path pattern `docs/{section}/{page}/{filename}`:

```markdown
![Alt text](https://assets.planton.ai/site/images/docs/{section}/{page}/{filename}.png)
```

### Examples

```markdown
![Deployment environments](https://assets.planton.ai/site/images/docs/ci-cd/deployment-environments/service-showing-deployment-environments.png)

![Infra job overview](https://assets.planton.ai/site/images/docs/infrastructure/infra-jobs/infra-job-running-state.png)
```

### Other Content Areas

| Content Area | Path Pattern |
|---|---|
| Docs | `docs/{section}/{page}/{filename}` |
| Blog | `blog/{post-slug}/{filename}` |
| Landing page | `landing/{filename}` |

## Image Upload Workflow

1. Place images in `site/content/assets/images/` following the same directory structure
2. Run `make sync-media` to compress and upload to Cloudflare R2
3. Reference using the full CDN URL in Markdown

For the detailed image processing pipeline, see `site/content/assets/_rules/process-planton-ai-images.mdc`.

## Naming Conventions

- Lowercase letters, hyphens for separators
- Descriptive, context-rich filenames
- Include relevant identifiers when helpful

Good: `kubernetes-dashboard-overview.png`, `infra-job-running-state.png`, `service-showing-deployment-environments.png`

Bad: `Screenshot_2026_03_05.png`, `IMG_1234.png`, `MyDashboard.png`, `dashboard pic.png`

## Requirements

- Always use the full `https://assets.planton.ai/site/images/...` URL
- Always include descriptive alt text
- No local paths (`/images/...`)
- No GitHub raw URLs
- No protocol-relative URLs — use `https://` explicitly
